UX/UI only (no auth/API/validation/redirect changes). Re-orders the visual weight
so the eye goes logo → headline → form → button → ZI:
- Grid rebalanced to ~55% form / ~45% ZI, tops aligned, with a much larger gap
  between the two zones; a soft white pool sits behind the form.
- Headline is larger, bolder and darker (leads the screen); lede + field labels
  get stronger contrast; the purple sign-in button is the only bold purple.
- Form tightened ~15% (shorter card, 52px inputs, smaller field gaps), width 460px;
  logo shrunk ~28% and pulled closer to the headline.
- ZI reduced to a supporting ~350–390px, nudged outward from the form, whole body
  and access card visible, halo greatly softened.
- Removed the "ZI כבר מחכה" label AND both activity chips (WhatsApp / deal) so
  nothing reads like an open task before sign-in.
- Background calmed: fainter grid/skyline/particles, quiet white area behind the form.
Fits 100vh without scroll at 1366×768 and 1440×900; RTL; mobile stack unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
